\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1\cf0 .  Come, O come, Thou quick'ning Spirit.
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Thou for ever art divine
\par Let Thy power never fail me,
\par always fill this heart of mine;
\par thus shall grace and truth and light
\par then dispel the gloom of night
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Grant in mind and in affections,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 wisdom, counsel purity
\par That I may be ever seeking
\par naught but that which pleases Thee
\par Let Thy knowledge spread and grow,
\par human errors over throw.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.    Always let us have assurance
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 that we are Thy children dear
\par Grant Thy wisdom in abundance
\par e'en thro' pain and anguish here.
\par for Thy loving Father's hand
\par leads us home as Thou has planned.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.   Holy Spirit, strong and mighty,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Thou who makest all things new,
\par make Thy Work within me perfect;
\par help me by Thy word so true.
\par Arm me with that sword of Thine
\par and the vict'ry shall be mine!\f1 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

